<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  LaunchAgent that keeps this fleet worker's own dashboard (`sdlc dashboard` bound to
  its tailnet address) running beside the worker — Story 35.4-006. The XPS
  dashboard relays a remote run's stories, stages, events and cost from it, so
  it must be up whenever com.fxmartin.sdlc-worker.plist is (that agent
  advertises this one with its dashboard-url argument).

  A sibling agent rather than a child of the worker: a worker restart (it exits
  75 on every controller upgrade) must not blank the XPS's view of the runs it
  is finishing, and a dashboard crash must not take jobs down with it.

  Substitute the three __PLACEHOLDERS__ below (launchd expands neither `~` nor
  `$VARS`); __TAILNET_IP__ and the port must match the worker's dashboard-url:

    __HOME__        the account's home, e.g. /Users/fxmartin
    __USER__        the account's login, for nix-darwin's per-user profile on PATH
    __TAILNET_IP__  this Mac's tailnet address (`tailscale ip -4`)

  Install:

    mkdir -p ~/.local/state/sdlc
    ip=$(tailscale ip -4)
    sed -e "s|__HOME__|$HOME|g" -e "s|__USER__|$USER|g" \
        -e "s|__TAILNET_IP__|${ip:?tailscale ip -4 printed no address}|g" \
        templates/launchd/com.fxmartin.sdlc-dashboard.plist \
        > ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.fxmartin.sdlc-dashboard.plist
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.fxmartin.sdlc-dashboard.plist

  `tailscale ip -4` prints nothing while Tailscale is stopped or logged out, and the
  ${ip:?} stops the install there, before it writes an agent: a blank host would
  bind every interface (`sdlc dashboard` refuses one as well).

  It binds the tailnet address only, never 0.0.0.0: the dashboard has no login of
  its own, so the tailnet ACL is its access control (XPS → M3 Max is trusted →
  trusted; XPS → home-lab needs tcp:8787). XDG_STATE_HOME is pinned to the
  worker's so it reads the same registry and ledgers its runs land in.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.fxmartin.sdlc-dashboard</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>__HOME__/.local/bin/sdlc</string>
    <string>dashboard</string>
    <string>--host</string>
    <string>__TAILNET_IP__</string>
    <string>--port</string>
    <string>8787</string>
  </array>

  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>__HOME__/.local/bin:/etc/profiles/per-user/__USER__/bin:/run/current-system/sw/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    <key>XDG_STATE_HOME</key>
    <string>__HOME__/.local/state</string>
  </dict>

  <!-- Start at login. KeepAlive covers a crash; the throttle keeps a missing
       tailnet address (the bind fails until Tailscale is up) from spinning.
       Unlike the worker, the dashboard has no exit on a controller reinstall:
       it serves the old code until
       `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.fxmartin.sdlc-dashboard`. -->
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <true/>
  <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
  <integer>30</integer>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>__HOME__/.local/state/sdlc/dashboard.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>__HOME__/.local/state/sdlc/dashboard.log</string>

  <!-- A read-only viewer: it should never compete with a build for CPU. -->
  <key>ProcessType</key>
  <string>Background</string>
</dict>
</plist>
